pi-python-core is an independent Python implementation, not an official Pi release.
Agent execution and transcript behavior are adapted from earendil-works/pi:
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/tree/a13d35a742c6ef8462812a28fbe1d8c8b7431c32
Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner. MIT license; see LICENSE.
The complete upstream source is fetched only for development under reference/pi.
Provider request conversion (Claude Messages, OpenAI and Codex Responses), the cached
WebSocket continuation, transcript replay helpers and the context estimate/shortHash in
src/pi_python/estimate.py are adapted from packages/ai of the same commit.

Selected provider, identity, timing, template and estimate behavior follows Pi v1.4.0:
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/tree/4a080252f06caf63a525d7873c5d94d3c23887e0
Selected later fixes and exact source hashes are documented in docs/UPSTREAM_FOLLOWUP.md
and reference/followup/. The original core-loop reference remains unchanged.
